<databaseChangeLog xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.1.xsd">

    <!--
        Task 9 removes the "Post Interest For Dynamic Deposit" standalone job (registered by
        0010_advancly_add_dynamic_deposit_post_interest_job.xml, Task 7) - DynamicDepositPostInterestTasklet/
        DynamicDepositPostInterestConfig no longer exist; Dynamic Deposit accounts are now posted from the same
        "Post Interest For Savings" run instead (see AdvanclySavingsSchedularInterestPoster#postDynamicDepositAccountsOnce).

        This is an ADDITIVE changeset, not an edit to 0010 - 0010 already ran (and inserted the row) on any
        environment that has been on Task 7+ before this change landed, and Liquibase changesets are never
        re-executed once applied, so editing 0010 in place would have no effect there. Following this custom
        module's own established "additive changeset, never edit an applied one" convention (see e.g. 0015/0016
        renaming existing tables via new changesets rather than rewriting the changesets that created them).

        job_run_history/job_parameters both hold a `RESTRICT` foreign key on job.id (see fineract-provider's
        0001_initial_schema.xml changesets 981/714), so any run-history/parameter rows for this job must be removed
        first, or the final delete from `job` would fail with a foreign-key-constraint violation on any environment
        where this job actually executed at least once.
    -->
    <changeSet author="advancly" id="1">
        <sql>
            delete from job_run_history where job_id in (select id from job where short_name = 'DD_PINT');
            delete from job_parameters where job_id in (select id from job where short_name = 'DD_PINT');
            delete from job where short_name = 'DD_PINT';
        </sql>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
